description:
CONTEXT BLOCK:

- **File/Function:** `chunk.rs` - missing tests for edge cases
- **The Smell:** No tests for: documents with no H2 headings, documents shorter than target tokens, documents with only H1, very large documents (>10k tokens), Unicode handling in chunk boundaries. Could cause empty chunks, oversized chunks, lost content, incorrect boundaries.

SPECIFICATION BLOCK (The "One-Shot" Instructions):

1. **EARS (Easy Approach to Requirements Syntax):**
   - When documents have no H2 headings, the system shall create single chunk with full content.
   - When documents are shorter than target tokens, the system shall create one appropriately-sized chunk.
   - When documents have Unicode at boundaries, the system shall respect UTF-8 character boundaries.
   - When all edge case tests pass, chunking shall be robust.

2. **DbC (Design by Contract):**
   - **Preconditions:**
     - Documents may have no sections (no H2)
     - Documents may be very short (<100 tokens)
     - Documents may be very long (>10,000 tokens)
     - Content may have multi-byte UTF-8 characters
   - **Postconditions:**
     - All chunks non-empty
     - No content lost
     - Chunk boundaries respect UTF-8
     - Token counts approximately target

3. **Schema & Edge Cases:**
   - **Test Cases Needed:**
     ```rust
     #[test] fn test_chunk_no_h2_headings()
     #[test] fn test_chunk_very_short_document()
     #[test] fn test_chunk_only_h1_no_sections()
     #[test] fn test_chunk_very_long_document()
     #[test] fn test_chunk_unicode_boundaries()
     #[test] fn test_chunk_empty_sections()
     #[test] fn test_chunk_table_preservation()
     ```
   - **Edge Cases:**
     - No H2 → single chunk
     - Only H1 → single chunk
     - Very short → one chunk < target size
     - Very long → multiple chunks
     - Unicode emoji → don't split mid-character

IMPLEMENTATION:

```rust
#[cfg(test)]
mod edge_case_tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn test_chunk_no_h2_headings() {
        let content = "# Title\n\nLong content without any H2 headings.\n\n".repeat(100);
        let chunks = create_chunks_at_level(&content, "doc1", "Test", ChunkLevel::Standard);

        assert!(!chunks.is_empty(), "Should create at least one chunk");
        assert!(chunks[0].content.contains("Title"), "Should include H1");
        // Should split on token count even without H2
        if content.split_whitespace().count() > 512 {
            assert!(chunks.len() > 1, "Long content should split");
        }
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_chunk_very_short_document() {
        let content = "# Short\n\nJust a few words.";
        let chunks = create_chunks_at_level(&content, "doc1", "Short", ChunkLevel::Standard);

        assert_eq!(chunks.len(), 1, "Short doc should be one chunk");
        assert!(chunks[0].token_count < 512, "Should be under target");
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_chunk_only_h1_no_sections() {
        let content = "# Title\n\nContent here.\n\n# Another Title\n\nMore content.";
        let chunks = create_chunks_at_level(&content, "doc1", "Test", ChunkLevel::Standard);

        assert!(!chunks.is_empty());
        // Verify content not lost
        let all_content: String = chunks.iter().map(|c| &c.content).collect();
        assert!(all_content.contains("Title"));
        assert!(all_content.contains("Another Title"));
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_chunk_very_long_document() {
        let long_content = "# Title\n\n## Section\n\n".to_string() + &"word ".repeat(10000);
        let chunks = create_chunks_at_level(&long_content, "doc1", "Long", ChunkLevel::Standard);

        assert!(chunks.len() > 1, "Long doc should split into multiple chunks");

        // Verify no content lost
        let total_words: usize = chunks.iter()
            .map(|c| c.content.split_whitespace().count())
            .sum();
        let original_words = long_content.split_whitespace().count();
        assert!(total_words >= original_words - 100, "Most words preserved");
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_chunk_unicode_boundaries() {
        let content = "# Unicode\n\n## Section\n\n";
        let emoji_content = "emoji 😀 ".repeat(1000);
        let full_content = content.to_string() + &emoji_content;

        let chunks = create_chunks_at_level(&full_content, "doc1", "Unicode", ChunkLevel::Standard);

        // Verify all chunks are valid UTF-8
        for chunk in &chunks {
            assert!(chunk.content.is_char_boundary(0));
            assert!(chunk.content.is_char_boundary(chunk.content.len()));
        }

        // Verify emojis not split
        let all_content: String = chunks.iter().map(|c| &c.content).collect();
        assert_eq!(
            all_content.matches('😀').count(),
            emoji_content.matches('😀').count(),
            "Emojis should be preserved"
        );
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_chunk_empty_sections() {
        let content = "# Title\n\n## Empty\n\n## Another Empty\n\n## Has Content\n\nSome text.";
        let chunks = create_chunks_at_level(&content, "doc1", "Test", ChunkLevel::Standard);

        assert!(!chunks.is_empty());
        // Empty sections might be skipped or included with minimal content
    }

    #[test]
    fn test_chunk_table_preservation() {
        let content = r#"# Title

## Table Section

| Col1 | Col2 |
|------|------|
| A    | B    |
| C    | D    |

More content."#;

        let chunks = create_chunks_at_level(&content, "doc1", "Table", ChunkLevel::Standard);

        let has_table = chunks.iter().any(|c| c.content.contains("| Col1 |"));
        assert!(has_table, "Table should be preserved in chunks");
    }
}
```
